gano - a simple console text editor written in GNU Guile
========================================================

Running
-------

Requires Guile 3.0.  From the source tree:

    bin/gano [FILE]

The first run byte-compiles the modules into Guile's cache, which takes
a minute; later starts are quick.

Keys (M- means Alt, or Esc then the key):

    arrows, Home/End, PgUp/PgDn   move (also ^A/^E, ^Y/^V)
    Backspace, Delete             delete (joining lines at line ends)
    Enter, Tab                    split the line, insert a tab
    ^K / ^U                       cut line / paste (consecutive cuts
                                  are pasted together)
    M-U / M-E                     undo / redo
    ^W                            search (ignores case, wraps around;
                                  Enter at the prompt repeats the last)
    ^_ or M-G                     go to line[,column]
    ^S                            save (asks for a name if there is none)
    ^O                            write out under a new name
    ^X                            exit (offers to save unsaved changes)
    ^Q                            exit, discarding unsaved changes
    ^C                            show the cursor position; at a prompt,
                                  cancel

Testing
-------

    test/run-all.sh              # every suite, one summary line each
    test/run-all.sh editor       # just test/test-editor.scm

Layout
------

    bin/gano                launcher script
    src/gano/editor.scm     the editor: state, key handling, screen
    src/gano/buffer.scm     one import for the character buffer layers
    src/gano/cbuf-*.scm     the character buffer (core, basic, standard,
                            extra, serialization, utils)
    src/gano/frame.scm      viewport onto a buffer
    src/gano/terminal.scm   raw mode, ANSI output, key input
    src/gano/keys.scm       key objects
    src/gano/text-metrics.scm, uax9-*.scm, char.scm, wcwidth.scm, ...
                            Unicode text measurement and bidi support
    attic/                  earlier experiments, kept for reference
